Give the user session a TZ, as login(1) and sshd do on illumos.

The session worker builds the session environment from scratch, so TZ
(set for gdm by init from /etc/default/init) did not reach the session.
libc's localtime() still finds the zone in /etc/default/init, but GLib's
GTimeZone only looks at TZ and /etc/localtime (absent on illumos) and
falls back to UTC: the GNOME clock and every GDateTime showed UTC.

Take TIMEZONE= from /etc/default/login when set (login(1)'s key), else
gdm's own TZ. Needs 0006-etc-default-login.patch (gdm_read_default).

--- a/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c	2026-11-11 08:44:02.776290764 +0100
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c	2026-11-11 08:44:02.891208008 +0100
@@ -1920,6 +1920,25 @@
 
 	gdm_session_worker_set_environment_variable (worker, "PATH", path_str);
 
+#ifdef __sun
+        /*
+         * Like login(1) and sshd: give the session a TZ, from TIMEZONE= in
+         * /etc/default/login, else gdm's own (init's, /etc/default/init).
+         * GLib's GTimeZone does not read /etc/default/init and falls back
+         * to UTC without TZ.
+         */
+        if (!gdm_session_worker_environment_variable_is_set (worker, "TZ")) {
+                g_autofree char *tz_str = gdm_read_default ("TIMEZONE=");
+
+                if (tz_str == NULL || tz_str[0] == '\0') {
+                        g_free (tz_str);
+                        tz_str = g_strdup (g_getenv ("TZ"));
+                }
+                if (tz_str != NULL && tz_str[0] != '\0')
+                        gdm_session_worker_set_environment_variable (worker, "TZ", tz_str);
+        }
+#endif
+
         if (! _change_user (worker, uid, gid)) {
                 g_debug ("GdmSessionWorker: Unable to change to user");
                 error_code = PAM_SYSTEM_ERR;
